<BaseLayout title="Privacy / Website Use" description="Privacy and website-use information for the Lowcountry Digital Works public website.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container readable"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy / Website Use</p><h1>A deliberately simple public website.</h1><p class="lede">This site is designed to provide business information without adding unnecessary tracking or data collection.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container readable">
<h2>Website data</h2><p>Lowcountry Digital Works does not intentionally use advertising trackers, behavioral analytics, nonessential cookies, customer accounts, or a public contact-form processor on this site.</p>
<h2>Hosting and security</h2><p>Infrastructure providers may process basic request and security metadata needed to deliver and protect the website. Those systems are separate from any future client-data service.</p>
<h2>Email</h2><p>Selecting an email link opens your email service. The website itself does not process that message. Do not send credentials, authentication material, payment-card information, PHI, or other sensitive secrets through an ordinary initial email.</p>
<h2>External services</h2><p>If future site features require additional data processing, their purpose, provider, and privacy implications should be evaluated before deployment and this notice should be updated as appropriate.</p>
<h2>Website use</h2><p>Public information on this site describes Lowcountry Digital Works as it currently operates and is not intended to create guarantees, certifications, or service commitments beyond an agreed engagement.</p>
<p><em>Last updated: August 10, 2026.</em></p>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
